# The first part of T-028: the registration, the identity, the door order,
# the MASQUE session over HTTP/2 and the rules. podnet holds src/warp/ to
# fixes from 7c5f87e (PodUtils/podnet#449); the one change after it
# (83e0c93, session.rs) names the meter of pod-relay; the relay leg comes
# with T-336. The other files of src/warp/ come with the entries of
# the rest of T-028 (TODO/adapters.md): l4.rs (T-406), live.rs, pod.rs,
# find.rs, route.rs, tun.rs, exit.rs.
# mod.rs: WarpClient becomes Warp (warp.rs, open.rs); the race of the
# direct path and the relay, and the leg file (T-336): open_session in
# open.rs, relay_first_from and the text of write_leg in leg.rs, the relay a
# dial of the caller (C137). WireGuard, the carry and the scan stay with
# their entries.
# h3.rs, wg.rs, session.rs and mod.rs (T-337): MASQUE over HTTP/3 on the
# endpoint of pod-quic over the caller's Datagrams (Way::h3, Way::udp); the
# driver of WireGuard over a Datagrams (wg.rs; Peer::from_exported stays
# with export.rs); connect_h3, connect_wg, connect_wg_inside and the
# halves of each transport (session.rs, session/); connect_carried and
# CARRY_MTU (carry.rs, warp.rs); HTTP/3 and WireGuard take no relay
# (open.rs). The tests of h3.rs and of session.rs go to src/h3/tests.rs
# and tests/h3.rs; the stand-in of wg/standin.rs is pod-wg's.
# session.rs (T-336): relay_budget; the meter of the relay is a function of
# the caller (Way::meter), as C173 decided for the budget.
# connect_outer: the check of the data path and the bad door (net.rs).
# ip.rs (T-335): its driver is the stack of pod-netstack (C138); its
# settings (--cc, the TCP burst, the TCP buffer, the counters of the link,
# the budget of a relay) are NetSettings (net/settings.rs), with its tests
# the_congestion_controller and the_tcp_burst_variable_is_checked; the
# controller, the burst and the shared counters are fields of StackConfig of
# pod-netstack (its SOURCES).
# proxy.rs (T-335, T-338): check_data_path and query_at are check.rs; the
# resolvers (Resolver, exchange_any, dot_exchange, forward_dns_to, query)
# are resolver.rs; handle_client_auth is proxy/client.rs; route and direct
# are proxy/route.rs; the UDP associations are proxy/udp.rs; the rest of
# run, client_on, STATS and admit are proxy.rs (values of the caller, no
# global); the unit tests are proxy/tests.rs, resolver.rs and
# tests/proxy.rs. bind, bind_all, health_log (a task of the caller over
# Proxy::health) stay in podnet; so do the tests
# a_unix_socket_that_answers_is_not_taken and
# a_refused_tcp_listener_does_not_stop_the_unix_socket (C201).
# proxy/names.rs (T-338): order, resolve and resolve_all are Names
# (proxy/names.rs), the pins a function of the caller; the test
# the_stack_takes_the_ipv6_address_of_an_ipv4_tunnel is of
# net/settings.rs.
# nc.rs (T-338): via_running, via_relay, pipe, git_ssh_command and
# ssh_config stay in podnet, with the tests the_ssh_config_uses_warp_nc and
# the_printed_block_quotes_the_path_as_the_written_block (C203);
# udp_via_running is udp_via_stream on a stream that the caller opens.
# services.rs of podnet-core: its module `warp`, tunnel_resolver and
# check_name (service.rs).
# rules.rs of podnet-netns: only Net, domain_matches, in_cidr and load_nets
# (rules/matcher.rs); the lint (rules/shadow.rs) stays in podnet and comes
# in as a function of the caller (PodUtils/podnet#452).
# l4.rs and proxy.rs run_l4 (T-406): L4 over h3::open and the UdpWay of the
# caller, Form in place of PODNET_WARP_L4_FORM, Warp::l4 (mod.rs l4);
# run_l4 is Proxy::over_l4 (proxy.rs, proxy/route.rs). The tests of l4.rs
# go to src/l4/tests.rs and tests/l4.rs.
